{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 1.0,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_supply",
      "components": ["U4", "J3"],
      "pins": ["U4.3", "J3.2"],
      "nets": ["+3V3"],
      "observed": "U4 pin 3 (T+) and J3 pin 2 are both connected to the +3V3 net. There is no dedicated net connecting J3 pin 2 to U4 pin 3.",
      "expected": "U4 pin 3 (T+) should connect directly to J3 pin 2, isolated from the +3V3 supply, as the other thermocouple channels do (J1.2–U2.3, J2.2–U3.3).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U4\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"T+\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J3\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "Thermocouple wire pair connects to a 2-pin screw terminal (J1 for U2, J2 for U3, J3 for U4) whose two pins wire directly to the MAX31855's differential thermocouple inputs T+ (pin 3) and T- (pin 2)."
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The third thermocouple channel (U4/J3) is nonfunctional. T+ is tied to 3.3V, so the MAX31855 will read an invalid differential voltage and likely report a fault. J3 pin 2 also presents 3.3V on the thermocouple connector, which could damage the thermocouple or the MAX31855 if connected. Firmware will see a thermocouple fault for zone 3 and abort runs.",
      "confidence": 1.0
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The design files contain a clear anomaly: the third thermocouple channel's T+ input (U4.3) and its connector pin (J3.2) are tied to the +3V3 supply instead of being connected to each other, which will make that channel nonfunctional and likely cause faults."
}

